{"evidence":["`cargo test -p tank_core systems::substrate::tests:: -- --nocapture` passed: 15 substrate-zone unit tests green.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load -- --nocapture` passed: 34 save/load tests green, including the O2-penetration round-trip and legacy-load cases.","`cargo test -p tank_core --test habitat_registry -- --nocapture` passed: 33 habitat-registry tests green.","`cargo test -p tank_scenarios --test geometry_scaling -- --nocapture` passed: 18 geometry-scaling tests green.","Source inspection shows the initialization path never normalizes zones: [substrate.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs#L357), [state.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L57), [state.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L115), and [engine.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs#L115)."],"findings_or_gaps":["High: fresh states are not initialized with computed oxic/suboxic zone state. [substrate.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs#L357) seeds every new layer as fully oxic, [state.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L57) and [state.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L115) only refresh habitats, and [engine.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs#L115) exposes that state through `Engine::new` without running `step_substrate_zones`. Any caller that inspects a new state or engine before the first hourly tick gets a stale fully oxic bed and no `SubstrateDeep` habitat, which is not the steady-state zone model this bead was meant to add.","High: multi-layer constructors write per-layer local depths into a field that the runtime now interprets as one shared stack boundary. [lib.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs#L972) and [state.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L119) store each layer's own depth in `o2_penetration_depth_cm`, but [state.rs](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs#L210) resolves the canonical boundary with `min()`. For the shipped `medium_planted` preset ([medium_planted.toml](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/scenarios/medium_planted.toml#L4), [active_planted.toml](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/active_planted.toml#L3), [coarse_porous.toml](/home/master/p/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/coarse_porous.toml#L3)), the raw state therefore defaults to a 4 cm boundary instead of a normalized stack value until a recompute happens.","Coverage gap: the new tests all exercise explicit `step_substrate_zones` or `Engine::from_parts` paths, but there is no regression test for `TankState::new`, `Engine::new`, or direct scenario materialization. That leaves the stale-constructor behavior above untested."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["Normalize substrate zones before exposing any ready-to-use state: call `step_substrate_zones` before `refresh_habitat_registry` in constructor/materialization paths (`TankState::new`, `TankState::seeded_example`, scenario builders, and any other public state factory), or seed the negative sentinel and force normalization before first use.","Stop persisting per-layer local depths into `o2_penetration_depth_cm` for multi-layer presets/builders. Write a shared boundary value or the uncomputed sentinel instead, and consider repairing positive-but-inconsistent current-schema payloads on load rather than only fixing negative-sentinel legacy saves.","Add regression tests that construct a fresh `TankState`, a fresh `Engine`, and a raw multi-layer scenario state (for example `medium_planted`) and assert that oxic/suboxic geometry plus `SubstrateSurface`/`SubstrateDeep` habitat mapping are already correct before the first simulated hour."],"outcome":"request_changes"}